  "notices": [
    "Review level is unreviewed and stage is partner-preview: no production support commitment attaches to this component version.",
    "Public release: https://github.com/Cork-Technology/rollover/releases/tag/v0.1.0-rc.2. The body is the frozen G10 deployment-address record and links the tag-specific manifest.",
    "The public source pin is commit cd8999a17e6ea679ad958c59fec584eaf29cfd25; deployed bytecode was compiled from private commit 5af1048eb9896582115c3615bdc5a4a9166cbbf6, which remains recorded in every deployment row.",
    "The paired Arbitrum/Base deployment vector, artifact digests, addresses and runtime hashes come from the tag-specific deployment manifest and reviewed plan source-plan-reviewed.json (plan digest sha256:81b2ae8552100ccec0f7388664ee662e4c656c5315d4f77b279336a0ce76334d) built with solc 0.8.34, Cancun, via-IR and optimizer runs=1.",
    "ExactSettler and PartialSettler use identical deterministic addresses on both chains but have chain-specific runtime hashes; each chain row pins its own observed runtime.",
    "BaseFiller is included as an operational singleton. EvcRolloverAdapter and per-holder CorkRolloverContract clones remain outside this component pin.",
    "No real two-chain cross-component integration runner exists for this cut; phoenix/v0.3-rc.1 records the explicit owner waiver and makes no passing rollover claim."
  ],
